    arm (1 of 2) lands inside 10% of a law fitted before it was run, so
    the period does track tau_a -- at 3.56 ms per ms with a fixed 180 ms
    latency that is NOT tau_a's. The log-log exponent of ~1.0 this line
    has demanded for four runs cannot be reached by any oscillator with a
    finite rise time, so that test was the wrong SHAPE rather than a
    failed mechanism. On one arm this is SUGGESTIVE, not settled.

